            "result_text": "Perfect! The regex is working correctly. Here's what the pattern does:\n\n**Key components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 validation** - Matches 0-255 for each octet without leading zeros\n   - `25[0-5]` → 250-255\n   - `2[0-4][0-9]` → 200-249  \n   - `1[0-9]{2}` → 100-199\n   - `[1-9]?[0-9]` → 0-99\n\n2. **Date validation** - Validates month-day combinations:\n   - Months 01,03,05,07,08,10,12 (31-day): days 01-31\n   - Months 04,06,09,11 (30-day): days 01-30\n   - Month 02 (February): days 01-29\n\n3. **Line requirement** - Lookahead ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n\n4. **Last date only** - Negative lookahead prevents matching if another valid date exists later on the line\n\n5. **Word boundaries** - `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])` and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9])` ensure dates and IPs aren't embedded in alphanumeric strings\n\nThe test results confirm all requirements are met:\n- ✅ Matches last date when multiple exist\n- ✅ Requires IPv4 on the line\n- ✅ Rejects invalid dates and IPs\n- ✅ Prevents false matches with proper boundaries"
